{"dependencies":["Not","Decidable.isFalse","Decidable","UInt64.ofBitVec","BitVec","UInt64.decEq._proof_1","OfNat.ofNat","UInt64","UInt64.decEq._proof_2","UInt64.decEq.match_1","Nat","instOfNatNat","Eq","dite","Decidable.isTrue","instDecidableEqBitVec"],"doc":"Decides whether two 64-bit unsigned integers are equal. Usually accessed via the\n`DecidableEq UInt64` instance.\n\nThis function is overridden at runtime with an efficient implementation.\n\nExamples:\n * `UInt64.decEq 123 123 = .isTrue rfl`\n * `(if (6 : UInt64) = 7 then \"yes\" else \"no\") = \"no\"`\n * `show (7 : UInt64) = 7 by decide`\n","extra":null,"kind":"definition","levels":[],"module":"Init.Prelude","name":"UInt64.decEq","nodes":[["constant","UInt64",[]],["constant","Decidable",[]],["constant","Eq",[["succ",["zero"]]]],["apply",2,0],["bound",1],["apply",3,4],["bound",0],["apply",5,6],["apply",1,7],["forall","b",0,8,"explicit"],["forall","a",0,9,"explicit"],["constant","UInt64.decEq.match_1",[["succ",["zero"]]]],["lambda","b._@.Init.Prelude.18944141._hygCtx._hyg.16",0,8,"explicit"],["lambda","a._@.Init.Prelude.18944141._hygCtx._hyg.14",0,12,"explicit"],["apply",11,13],["apply",14,4],["apply",15,6],["constant","BitVec",[]],["constant","OfNat.ofNat",[["zero"]]],["constant","Nat",[]],["apply",18,19],["natural","64"],["apply",20,21],["constant","instOfNatNat",[]],["apply",23,21],["apply",22,24],["apply",17,25],["constant","dite",[["succ",["zero"]]]],["constant","UInt64.ofBitVec",[]],["apply",28,4],["apply",3,29],["apply",28,6],["apply",30,31],["apply",1,32],["apply",27,33],["apply",2,26],["apply",35,4],["apply",36,6],["apply",34,37],["constant","instDecidableEqBitVec",[]],["apply",39,25],["apply",40,4],["apply",41,6],["apply",38,42],["constant","Decidable.isTrue",[]],["bound",2],["apply",28,45],["apply",3,46],["apply",47,29],["apply",44,48],["constant","UInt64.decEq._proof_1",[]],["apply",50,45],["apply",51,4],["apply",52,6],["apply",49,53],["lambda","h",37,54,"explicit"],["apply",43,55],["constant","Not",[]],["apply",57,37],["constant","Decidable.isFalse",[]],["apply",59,48],["constant","UInt64.decEq._proof_2",[]],["apply",61,45],["apply",62,4],["apply",63,6],["apply",60,64],["lambda","h",58,65,"explicit"],["apply",56,66],["lambda","m",26,67,"explicit"],["lambda","n",26,68,"explicit"],["apply",16,69],["lambda","b",0,70,"explicit"],["lambda","a",0,71,"explicit"]],"project":false,"range":{"column":0,"endColumn":82,"endLine":2686,"line":2669},"type":10,"typeText":"(a b : UInt64) → Decidable (Eq.{1} a b)","unsafe":false,"value":72,"source":{"code":"/--\nDecides whether two 64-bit unsigned integers are equal. Usually accessed via the\n`DecidableEq UInt64` instance.\n\nThis function is overridden at runtime with an efficient implementation.\n\nExamples:\n * `UInt64.decEq 123 123 = .isTrue rfl`\n * `(if (6 : UInt64) = 7 then \"yes\" else \"no\") = \"no\"`\n * `show (7 : UInt64) = 7 by decide`\n-/\n@[extern \"lean_uint64_dec_eq\"]\ndef UInt64.decEq (a b : UInt64) : Decidable (Eq a b) :=\n  match a, b with\n  | ⟨n⟩, ⟨m⟩ =>\n    dite (Eq n m)\n      (fun h => isTrue (h ▸ rfl))\n      (fun h => isFalse (fun h' => UInt64.noConfusion h' (fun h' => absurd h' h)))","start":2669,"end":2686},"axioms":[]}